From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: L1216 chain, dynamic strides and back macro calls keep draw reuse (EDEN_UP_L1216_CHAIN)

DRAFT, not built. Ports the final commit of zortos293/Lichii PR #1216 (@sanchodecuba11-del), on
0557. Gated by EDEN_UP_L1216_CHAIN (exact 1), a live switch (Id L1216Chain, not armed); off by
default. Does something only with EDEN_UP_L974_CHAIN=1 and EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1. The stride/enable
word (when vertex input is dynamic state) and the render enable addresses become draw
parameters; both are already exempt under 0441 with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_OOT_EXEMPT=1. A back macro
call (EDEN_UP_L1056_BACK_MACROS=1) is sent FastDrawNeutral when DmaReadCallIsNeutral(). Our 0485
DeferWords already carries the flags.

Reviewed draft from job J, v2: reviewer re-anchored the live_switch.h hunks, gated the back macro
flag with DmaReadCallIsNeutral(), added a fast draw break in macro.cpp before the inline DMA
read flushes GPU-written memory for a split_writes macro (the draft let handle words change with
no break), and fixed comment placement in nx2_fast_draw.h and vk_pipeline_cache.h.
